  "id": "chunk_17",
  "chunk": "The game is accessed through a browser-based implementation [14]. A custom-\nbuilt Python script connects the LLM and the game environment. The script\ncaptures the game’s output after each move, forwards it to the LLM, receives\nthe model’s command, and inputs this command back into the game. The LLM\nhas access to the full conversation of the current run.\nWe evaluate six LLM-based chatbots from three major providers:\n•Anthropic:Claude Opus 4.5 and Claude Sonnet 4.5, with an additional\nvariant of Opus 4.5 with ‘extended thinking’ enabled.\n•OpenAI:ChatGPT 5.2 in two configurations: ‘standard thinking’ and\n‘extended thinking’.\n•Google:Gemini 3 with ‘thinking’ enabled.\nEach model plays the game independently, with no informationexplicitly\nshared between runs or models. Each model does have access to previous chats\nwhich the model may or may not use in subsequent chats. Importantly, general-\npurpose LLMs have not been specifically trained or fine-tuned onZorkor similar",
